WEBVTT

00:11:58.980 --> 00:12:00.865
in the laboratory.

00:12:00.889 --> 00:12:04.020
And as endearingly as my dad
kind of notes this

00:12:04.044 --> 00:12:06.295
as being my, like, dragon-slayer moment,

00:12:06.319 --> 00:12:09.303
where I had risen up
and fought this behemoth

00:12:09.327 --> 00:12:11.226
and it caused this domino effect,

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:12.613
I can tell you right now,

00:12:12.637 --> 00:12:15.232
I felt anything but courageous.

00:12:15.623 --> 00:12:18.644
I was scared, I was terrified,

00:12:18.668 --> 00:12:20.487
I was anxious,

00:12:20.511 --> 00:12:23.541
I was ashamed, slightly,

00:12:23.565 --> 00:12:25.962
that it took me a month
to write the letter.

00:12:25.986 --> 00:12:27.716
There was a glimmer of hope in there

00:12:27.740 --> 00:12:30.391
that maybe somehow
no one would ever figure out